WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.165 --> 00:00:03.915
(upbeat instrumental music)

00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:30.680
- The three things that you
can do to close the wealth gap

00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:32.080
and fight for wealth justice:

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:35.130
vote, donate, intersectionality.

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:38.090
When we vote, we are electing people

00:00:38.090 --> 00:00:40.480
who will enact fiscal policy.

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:45.010
Fiscal policy is the way
that money gets allocated

00:00:45.010 --> 00:00:49.380
to certain things in our local,
state, and federal budgets.

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:52.740
We should donate to
organizations like BlackFem

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:55.230
because they tend to be
typically underfunded

00:00:55.230 --> 00:00:57.280
and they're doing the wealth justice work

00:00:57.280 --> 00:00:59.470
that is going to close the wealth gap

00:00:59.470 --> 00:01:01.490
for marginalized populations.

00:01:01.490 --> 00:01:03.840
And finally, and I think most importantly

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:05.950
because this is something
that we can hold ourselves

00:01:05.950 --> 00:01:07.490
accountable to every day,

00:01:07.490 --> 00:01:09.520
we have to think about wealth inequality

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:12.610
from an intersectional lens
across race and gender.

00:01:12.610 --> 00:01:15.870
For every dollar a single Black man owns

00:01:15.870 --> 00:01:18.770
a Black woman only owns 42 cents.

00:01:18.770 --> 00:01:22.080
So when we only tend to couch the idea

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:24.820
behind wealth inequality
in just one dimension,

00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:27.450
race, gender, or class,

00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:30.450
we actually are rendering
Black women's inequality

00:01:30.450 --> 00:01:33.350
that they experience from a
wealth perspective invisible.

00:01:33.350 --> 00:01:37.060
So the issues that show up in our society

00:01:37.060 --> 00:01:39.890
and the inequalities that
we're struggling against

00:01:39.890 --> 00:01:43.030
have to be met with
solutions that are aligned

00:01:43.030 --> 00:01:47.380
with the intersectionality
of our identities, our past,

00:01:47.380 --> 00:01:49.600
and what we ultimately want to see

00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:51.269
to be able to create change.

00:01:51.269 --> 00:01:55.019
(upbeat instrumental music)

